.TH CAMLET 1 "August 2026" "Camlet 0.2.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
camlet \- native floating camera overlay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B camlet
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Camlet is a lightweight, frameless, always-on-top camera overlay built with
Rust, Iced, and WGPU. Drag the camera with the left mouse button and open its
settings menu with the right mouse button.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --frame-source " " <real|synthetic>
Select the camera frame producer. The default is
.BR real .
.TP
.BR --profile-dir " " <directory>
Override the native settings directory.
.TP
.BR --screenshot " " <path.ppm>
Capture the native window over white and exit.
.TP
.B --automation-check
Validate the automation configuration and exit without opening a window.
.TP
.B --automation-exit
Open the window and close it automatically.
.TP
.BR --automation-script " " <file>
Run a validated unattended scenario.
.TP
.BR --automation-output " " <directory>
Write scenario readiness and results to the directory.
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Print command-line help.
.TP
.BR -V , " " --version
Print the application version.
.SH FILES
Camlet stores its settings in the platform-native user configuration directory.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/rayan6ms/camlet/issues.
.SH LICENSE
GPL-3.0-only.
